.TH BOSWAS-ARCHIVE-MANAGER 1 "November 2026" "boswas-apps 1.0~alpha3" "Boswas OS"
.SH NAME
boswas-archive-manager \- open, extract and create ZIP and TAR archives
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B boswas-archive-manager
.RI [ archive " ...]"
.br
.B boswas-archive-manager \-\-extract
.IR archive " ..."
.RB [ \-\-to
.IR folder ]
.br
.B boswas-archive-manager \-\-extract\-here
.IR archive " ..."
.br
.B boswas-archive-manager \-\-create
.I output file
\&...
.br
.B boswas-archive-manager
.BR \-\-help " | " \-\-version
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B boswas-archive-manager
is Archive Manager, the Boswas OS application for compressed archives. It
shows an archive like a folder: a path bar through the folders inside it, a
details list (name, size, packed size, modification time, type, checksum and
permission bits where the format stores them) that can be sorted and
searched, and a preview pane for text files and pictures. From there the
whole archive or the selected entries are extracted, files and folders are
added or deleted, the archive is tested for damage, and new archives are
created.
.PP
Without an option each
.I archive
opens in a window of its own. Every start of the program is its own process.
.PP
The program runs as the desktop user and refuses to start as root.
.SS Formats
.TP
.B Read and write
ZIP (also JAR, APK and EPUB files, which are ZIP archives), TAR, and TAR
compressed with gzip, bzip2 or xz.
.TP
.B Read
Single files compressed with gzip, bzip2 or xz (they extract to the
uncompressed file). ZIP entries encrypted with the legacy ZIP encryption are
read after asking for the password.
.TP
.B Read, with the 7zip package installed
7z archives, RAR archives (these also need the RAR codec of 7z, in Debian
the package
.BR 7zip\-rar )
and ZIP entries that use AES encryption or a compression method Python does
not have. Without the package these are shown as "needs the 7zip package".
.TP
.B Read, with a Zstandard module in Python
Files and TAR archives compressed with Zstandard (the module
.B zstandard
of the package python3\-zstandard, or
.B compression.zstd
of Python 3.14). Without one they are listed as not available.
.PP
A file is recognised by its content, not by its name. The 7z program is used
only to read: it lists an archive and writes the content of entries to a
pipe, with the password given on its standard input. It never writes a file.
.SS Extraction
Whatever an archive contains, extraction creates nothing outside the
destination folder:
.IP \(bu 3
An entry whose name has a
.B ..
component or a NUL character is not extracted. A leading
.B /
is dropped. Control characters in names are replaced by an underscore.
.IP \(bu 3
Every path is created component by component below the destination without
following symbolic links, so a link that is already in the destination, or
that the archive itself contains, is never written through. Files are written
under a temporary name and renamed into place.
.IP \(bu 3
Symbolic links are created last and only when their target stays inside the
destination; when all are in place each is resolved again and removed if it
leads outside through other links. Hard links are made only to files of the
same extraction.
.IP \(bu 3
Device nodes, pipes and sockets are skipped. Set-user-ID, set-group-ID and
sticky bits are dropped. Permission bits and modification times are kept, the
permission bits masked by the umask; folders always stay writable for their
owner. Owners are never changed.
.IP \(bu 3
Before extracting, and while writing data whose size the archive does not
announce, the amount is compared with limits: more than 8 GB, more than 200
times the size of the archive once above 256 MB, more than 500,000 entries,
or more than the free space. Beyond a limit a dialog states the numbers and
asks whether to continue.
.PP
For files that already exist the choices are to ask each time, replace, keep
the existing file, or keep both by adding a number to the new name. Two
entries with the same name in one archive: the later one is kept. Everything
that was skipped or failed is listed with its reason when the extraction ends.
.SS Creating and changing
New archives are ZIP (deflate, with a choice of compression level, or
stored), TAR, TAR.GZ, TAR.XZ or TAR.BZ2. Symbolic links are stored as links
or, on request, followed; hidden files can be left out; sockets, devices and
pipes are never packed. TAR archives are written without owner names and
numbers.
.PP
Adding to and deleting from a ZIP or TAR archive writes a new archive beside
the old one and renames it into place when it is complete. If that fails or
is cancelled, the original is unchanged. Password-protected and damaged
archives cannot be changed.
.SS Opening an entry
Opening a file from the list extracts it into a private folder below the
user's cache directory, read-only, and hands it to its default application;
changes are not written back. The folder is removed when the window closes.
Programs, scripts, installers and desktop entries are not opened from inside
an archive.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-extract
Extract each
.I archive
without showing its contents: into a folder named after the archive, beside
it
.RI ( photos.tar.gz
goes to
.IR photos ),
or into the folder given with
.BR \-\-to .
Only a progress window is shown; it asks for a password, about existing
files and about unusually large archives when needed, and closes when
everything was extracted. If something was left out it stays open and lists
it.
.TP
.BI \-\-to " folder"
With
.BR \-\-extract :
the folder to extract into. It is created if needed.
.TP
.B \-\-extract\-here
Extract each
.I archive
into the folder it is in, with the same progress window.
.TP
.B \-\-create
Pack every
.I file
(files and folders) into the new archive
.IR output ,
whose extension selects the format:
.BR .zip ", " .tar ", " .tar.gz " (" .tgz "), " .tar.xz " (" .txz ") or " .tar.bz2 " (" .tbz2 ")."
An existing
.I output
is replaced only after asking.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Show the usage and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Show the version and exit.
.PP
These three options are what the Files application calls from its context
menu.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or the window was closed normally.
.TP
.B 1
With
.BR \-\-extract ", " \-\-extract\-here " or " \-\-create :
something was skipped or failed.
.TP
.B 2
The operation was cancelled, or the command line was wrong.
.TP
.B 4
Started as root.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.ArchiveManager/state.json
Recent archives and the last choices in the extract dialog.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/com.boswas.ArchiveManager/window.ini
Size of the window.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/com.boswas.ArchiveManager/opened\-*
Entries that were opened from an archive; removed when the window closes.
.TP
.I /usr/share/applications/com.boswas.ArchiveManager.desktop
The desktop entry.
.TP
.IR /usr/bin/7z ", " /usr/bin/7zz ", " /usr/bin/7za
Where the optional 7z program is looked for.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tar (1),
.BR zip (1),
.BR unzip (1),
.BR 7z (1),
.BR boswas\-files (1)
